DESCRIPTION:<span>Often worshipers are asked to put away their devices dur
 ing worship service\, but you won’t hear that on <b><span>Social Media S
 unday\, the last Sunday in September</span></b>.<span> </span><i>Why?</i><
 span><i> </i></span>Because Jesus said so in Sunday's Gospel!<span> </spa
 n>Jesus reminds us to not "stand idle all day\;" so therefore\, use the to
 ols we have in 2023 to connect Holy Spirit with the world outside our four
  walls -- <i>via Social Media!</i><span><i> </i></span><b><span>People ne
 ed to be told the Good News multiple times in multiple ways</span></b>:in 
 person\, Facebook\, Instagram\, website\, letter\, etc. Each of us must <b
 ><span>share the Good News!</span></b></span><p><span>In 2023\, our <b><sp
 an>communication options include social media</span></b>.<span> </span>Wit
 h over 2.3 billion users of social media* around the globe and 1million ne
 w social mobile users added each day*\, going into the world to <b><span>s
