SUMMARY:Acolyte Training #1
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260927T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260927T120000
DTSTAMP:20260926T045335Z
UID:7806pv9ttesa394f6lnhg04tj5@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260927T113000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260921T193002Z
DESCRIPTION:<span><span>Is your child sixth grade or older? Would s/he lik
 e to be <b>an acolyte</b>?<i> A what? </i>According to <a href="https://ww
 w.episcopalchurch.org/glossary/acolyte/" target="_blank">The Episcopal Chu
 rch website</a>\, an acolyte is defined as "</span></span><span>A general 
 term which covers not only servers\, torchbearers\, and lighters of candle
 s but also crucifers\, thurifers\, and banner-bearers."</span><br><span><b
 r></span><span>At Holy Spirit Verona\, sixth to eighth grade students have
  a<b> Sunday School class offered twice a month</b>. On the non-class Sund
 ays\,<strong> sixth to 8th grade students </strong>are encouraged to be to
 rchbearers\, banner-bearers and second cross bearer at times on weeks when
  there is no junior/high school Sunday School Class. And on the non-class 
 Sundays\, <strong>ninth to twelfth grade students</strong> can be lead cr
 oss bearers at times if interested. Confirmation Students can use this tim
 e at "service" or "outreach hours."</span><br><span><br>We will host <b>tw
 o training sessions</b> this fall for new acolytes -- attendance at ONE se
 ssions is enough\, but if your child wants to attend both that works too! 
 <b>Meet at the Ushers' Table in the Sanctuary at 11:30am</b> on either/bot
 h Sundays (<b>September 27 or/and October 11</b>). If you have any questio
 ns\, speak with Danielle Mueller or Father Jerry. </span>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260921T194921Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Church of the Holy Spirit Verona
END:VEVENT
