BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Thespaceforart": "https://thespaceforart.com/event/reimagining-the-tarot-an-intuitive-collage-workshop/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:thespaceforart
X-SOURCE:The Space For Art
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260927T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260927T150000
DTSTAMP:20260917T172036Z
CREATED:20260823T223447Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260917T172036Z
UID:10184-1790512200-1790521200@thespaceforart.com
SUMMARY:* POSTPONED - Reimagining the Tarot:  An Intuitive Collage Workshop
DESCRIPTION:This month’s edition is postponed to a future date\, to be announced.  Please join our Tea & Tarot events in the meantime! \nWhat if the Tarot could speak in your voice? \nIn this exploratory workshop\, we’ll dive into the rich history and symbolism of the Major Arcana — exploring the colors\, archetypes\, and allegories that have given these iconic cards their power for centuries. Then\, we’ll turn that wisdom over to your own creative instincts. \nNo art experience needed. No tarot experience needed. Just an open mind and a willingness to listen to what’s stirring inside you. \nYou’ll choose a card that calls to you\, journal your reflections\, and then bring it to life through drawing\, painting\, or collage — reimagining it through your own symbols\, style\, and personal expression. The goal isn’t perfection; it’s presence. We’re letting intuition lead. \n📅 Sunday\, September 27 | 12:30 pm – 3:00 pm 📍 The Space\, 356 Bloomfield Ave\, Loft #2\, Montclair\, NJ 🎟 \n The first 1.5 hours is the lecture about the major arcana and symbolism for $45  \nReturning participants can choose to skip the lecture and arrive at 2:00 pm for $20 for the collage portion \nWhat You’ll Do: \n\nExplore the Major Arcana and the art of symbolic storytelling\nChoose a card that resonates with you in the moment\nJournal your insights and reflections\nSketch and plan your own symbolic design\nCreate your unique version of the card through your medium of choice.  Collage materials\, magazines\, paint\, colored pencils and markers will be available.\n\nAll materials provided. Just bring your imagination\, an open mind\, a tarot deck\, and a notebook. \nThis is an on-going series that allows you to build on your personal deck through repeated attendance. \n  \nYour Guide Gina Devine\nInstagram: @gina.devine \n\nGina Devine is an esoteric artist\, intuitive tarot reader\, writer\, educator and guide. \nShe has provided thousands of readings for people all over the world\, and leads both protection and tarot workshops. Her approach to guidance is loving\, grounded and human. Although she also teaches traditional tarot classes\, her tea and tarot discussion group was birthed from the knowing that people are more inclined to to be in tune with the archetypes of the cards and the messages they bring when they are allowed space to enjoy the tarot in a more casual setting – instead of forcefully trying to memorize them. The same way we find joy in discussing a book in community\, the cards also call for us to convene together around them. Her approach is philosophical\, therapeutic and creative\, and she is on a mission to guide people toward unearthing a more intimate and honest relationship with their inner knowing through the art of divination. You can find her services and more at soulcentrictarot.com \n\n👉 Sign up for the Soul Centric Tarot Newsletter
URL:https://thespaceforart.com/event/reimagining-the-tarot-an-intuitive-collage-workshop/
CATEGORIES:Art,Meditate and Create
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://thespaceforart.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/unnamed-4-e1787524194957.jpg
END:VEVENT
