UID:10274-1790514000-1790528400@thespaceforart.com
SUMMARY:Long Pose Figure Drawing and Painting
DESCRIPTION:Long Pose Figure Drawing and Painting \nCover art by Jake Yeh \nSunday\, September 27\, 1 – 5 pm\, $10 per hour or $35 for the full session \n“The object isn’t to make art\, it’s to be in that wonderful state which makes art inevitable.” – Robert Henri \nThis special Sunday session is an extended version of our beloved Tuesday night figure drawing\, giving you a full four hours to sink deep into the work. Bring your favorite materials\, settle in\, listen to some good tunes in great company\, and get into your flow.  This will be a great opportunity to create a more finished work of art\, hone your portraiture skills\, or work with a material that you don’t normally get to use. \nOur model will be dressed in character (more details coming soon) and serve as our muse for the afternoon.  Whether you want to loosen up your line work\, push into a sustained study\, or simply spend a slow Sunday afternoon drawing from life\, this is your space to do it. \nYou can stay for the full session\, or drop in and pay by the hour for an hour or two. \nAll skill levels welcome\, from seasoned studio artists to total beginners. Even poets have been known to drop in. \nMaterials such as charcoal\, graphite\, ink\, pastels\, and paints are all welcome. Basic drawing supplies available upon request. No formal instruction is given so it is a self-guided session. \nCheck out our regular weekly Tuesday night sessions here.
URL:https://thespaceforart.com/event/long-pose-figure-drawing-and-painting/
LOCATION:the Space\, 356 Bloomfield Ave\, Montclair\, New Jersey\, 07042
CATEGORIES:Art,Figure Drawing
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://thespaceforart.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/20260607_173108-scaled-e1787348554319.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Unioncong": "https://www.unioncong.org/event/anti-semitism-training-offsite/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:unioncong
X-SOURCE:Union Congregational Church
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260927T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260927T170000
DTSTAMP:20260926T005404
CREATED:20260318T124221Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260828T124812Z
UID:10003999-1790514000-1790528400@www.unioncong.org
SUMMARY:Dismantling Anti-Semitism (B'nai Keshet)
DESCRIPTION:This session will include individual and congregational storytelling by allied communities related to race\, antisemitism\, and white nationalism; grounding in skills like deep listening and constructive feedback; interactive analysis of the intertwined histories of racism and antisemitism; and contemporary challenges to interfaith solidarity movements. \nTo Register Click HERE  \nQuestions? Please reach out to Bnai Keshet member Jessica Brater or Rev. Katrina \nAbout the Facilitator \nMegan Black Johnson is a trainer\, facilitator\, and organizer who has spent much of her career trying to make sense of our differences and build bridges between them. Trained in community organizing and interfaith solidarity\, since 2010 Megan has worked with organizations like Interfaith America\, Faith in Action\, JOIN for Justice\, and Western States Center to navigate the divisions created by race\, religion\, and politics\, with a particular focus on the issues of antisemitism\, anti-Black racism\, and Christian hegemony. Megan earned her undergraduate degree from the University of Notre Dame and a Master of Divinity degree from Vanderbilt University. She now directs a program to counter antisemitism and protect democracy at Western States Center and regularly trains and facilitates bridge-building initiatives across the country. Megan and her husband (an ordained priest in the Episcopal church) are travel enthusiasts\, casual cyclists\, active in their Episcopal church community\, and proud\, exhausted parents of a toddler. They live in Baltimore\, Maryland. 
URL:https://www.unioncong.org/event/anti-semitism-training-offsite/
LOCATION:Temple B’nai Keshet\, 99 S Fullerton Ave\, Montclair\, NJ\, 07042\, United States
CATEGORIES:All Events,Featured Events,Justice & Community Engagement
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Montclairlocal": "https://montclairlocal.news/event/whats-up-with-kidlit-industry-experts-panel/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:montclairlocal
X-SOURCE:Montclair Local News
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260927T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260927T160000
DTSTAMP:20260729T030256Z
CREATED:20260729T030256Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T030256Z
UID:10140622-1790515800-1790524800@montclairlocal.news
SUMMARY:What's Up with KidLit? Industry Experts Panel
DESCRIPTION:What’s Up with KidLit? Industry experts on crafting stories for young readers \nFrom enchanting picture books to riveting young adult novels\, books have the power to turn young people into lifelong readers. But children’s literature has also become a battleground in the culture wars\, readership is in deep decline\, and AI is everywhere. What is the state of children’s literature today? And what will make your story stand out from the crowd? \nThis panel features three industry professionals with comprehensive knowledge of the field. Our discussion will provide candid insights into the current children’s literary landscape\, evolving children’s publishing trends\, and provide practical tips for aspiring writers and insights for parents and educators into the unique challenges and opportunities of children’s publishing today. \nIf you want a clear understanding of how books make a difference\, and how yours can stand out in a competitive field\, join us. \nPANELISTS:\nMaria Russo is an Editor-at-Large at Union Square Kids\, an imprint of Grand Central Publishing\, part of Hachette Book Group. Previously she was an Editorial Director at Astra Books for Young Readers. Maria also worked for many years as a cultural journalist\, including five years as Children’s Books Editor of The New York Times Book Review. She is the co-author of How to Raise a Reader (Workman) and lives in Montclair\, NJ. \nCarter Hasegawa has been in the children’s book world for over 20 years—as a book seller for various indies across the US\, as an editor at Candlewick Press\, and now\, as a literary agent with Tugeau 2 Art and Literary Agency. Originally from Seattle\, Carter now lives in Boston with his librarian wife and their two young sons. \nKat Brzozowski is a senior editor at Feiwel & Friends\, an imprint of Macmillan Children’s Publishing Group\, where she has worked since 2016 after seven years at St. Martin’s Press. She has edited a wide range of titles\, including the New York Times-bestselling picture I Love You More Than You’ll Ever Know by Leslie Odom Jr. and Nicolette Robinson\, with art by Joy Hwang Ruiz\, Anna-Marie McLemore’s When the Moon was Ours and The Mirror Season\, both longlisted for the National Book Award\, and new Fear Street books in R.L. Stine’s best-selling series\, which has sold over eighty million copies worldwide. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/whats-up-with-kidlit-industry-experts-panel/
LOCATION:Online – Virtual\, Montclair\, NJ\, 07042\, United States
CATEGORIES:General Events
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://montclairlocal.news/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/whats-up-with-kidlit-1.png
ORGANIZER;CN="The Writers Circle":MAILTO:info@writerscircleworkshops.com
END:VEVENT
