DTSTART:20261003T180000Z
DTEND:20261003T193000Z
DTSTAMP:20261003T000000Z
SUMMARY:Exploring Hispanic & Afro-Caribbean Genealogy
DESCRIPTION:About the program\n\nIf you are just starting out on your path 
 through family history\, this interactive and informative lecture\, 
 Introduction to Hispanic Genealogy\, is perfect for you. This approach\, 
 spearheaded by genealogist Irisneri Alicea Flores\, streamlines the 
 research process while shedding light on the cultural and historical 
 background of Puerto Rican and Hispanic descent more generally.\n\nBy 
 following a four-step process\, participants will be able to organize their 
 existing knowledge\, conduct interviews with family members\, locate 
 relevant family records\, and set specific research objectives for their 
 genealogical study. Using online genealogical platforms and historical 
 documents can overwhelm beginners\, but this presentation will help them 
 manage their emotions and avoid repeating mistakes.\n\nSpanish naming 
 customs\, historical jargon\, and cultural context discovered in records 
 are some of the research approaches that are exclusive to Hispanic and 
 Puerto Rican populations. Participants will gain self-assurance in their 
 genealogical work as the course covers typical research mistakes\, ways to 
 improve accuracy\, and practical procedures.\n\nAbout the 
 artist\n\nDescubre Tu Historia was founded by Irisneri Alicea Flores\, a 
 professional genealogist. Originating from Bayamón\, Puerto Rico\, she is 
 an authority on Latin American\, Caribbean\, and Puerto Rican genealogy. 
 She assists people in retracing their family trees by means of DNA 
 testing\, oral histories\, and archival research\; she has been doing this 
 work for over 13 years and has a Certificate in Genealogy Research from 
 Boston University.Irisneri\, who is fluent in both English and Spanish\, 
 has spoken about Hispanic ancestry at events hosted by museums\, 
 libraries\, and genealogical groups in the United States. Helping people 
 find\, keep\, and celebrate their family history is something she feels 
 strongly about.\n\n
LOCATION:West Orange - Community Room 1
ORGANIZER;CN="West Orange Library":MAILTO:events@westorange.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Lecture
UID:LibCal-10341-16729290
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16729290
END:VEVENT
