  how artificial intelligence is reshaping student experiences in research
  and literacy. As AI tools become embedded in academic work\, students mu
 st navigate questions of authorship\, credibility\, and learning processe
 s. Participants will explore how AI functions as both a research assistan
 t and a literacy tool\, shaping how students generate ideas\, gather info
 rmation\, and compose texts.\n\nHosted by: The ADP Center\n\nAdditional I
 nformation can be found at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event
 /12713139
