SUMMARY:Verona Interfaith Thanksgiving Service at B'nai Shalom West Orange
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261122T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261122T163000
DTSTAMP:20260926T045335Z
UID:5ebf61abgclqdirjiid7pdcl6k@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20261122T150000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260805T155322Z
DESCRIPTION:<span>The clergy leaders of five of Verona&#39\;s houses of wo
 rship and one in West Orange will host an Interfaith Thanksgiving Service.
  The service will include scripture readings from Jewish\, Islamic &amp\; 
 Christian traditions\, as well as music related to Thanksgiving with a joi
 nt choir from a few of the congregations. A light reception will follow.</
 span><p></p><p><i><span>Questions?</span></i><span> <span> </span>Contact
  any of the clergy leaders at the participating houses of worship: the <b>
 First Congregational Church of Verona\, </b>the <b>First Presbyterian Chur
 ch of Verona</b>\, <b>Our Lady of the Lake Roman Catholic Church</b>\, the
 <b> Islamic Center of Verona</b><span>\,</span><b> </b>the<b> Episcopal Ch
 urch of the Holy Spirit</b><span> and </span><b>B’nai Shalom West Orange
 </b><span>.</span></span></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260805T155323Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Church of the Holy Spirit Verona
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Peakperfs": "https://www.peakperfs.org/event/the-party-scene/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:peakperfs
X-SOURCE:PEAK Performances at MSU
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T173000
DTSTAMP:20260925T215355
CREATED:20260719T165705Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260812T001749Z
UID:6023-1795359600-1795368600@www.peakperfs.org
SUMMARY:The Hands Free & Dance Heginbotham: The Party Scene
DESCRIPTION:Exquisitely eclectic quartet The Hands Free and members of the fabulously whimsical Dance Heginbotham join forces in The Party Scene. Inspired by The Nutcracker and your holiday office party\, this music and dance extravaganza is part Drosselmeyer and part Turkey Lurkey Time. Lightly immersive and family friendly\, The Party Scene features student party guests from Montclair State University. All guests are encouraged to don impressively festive seasonal sweaters. \n \nAbout The Hands Free: The Hands Free is an acoustic quartet\, bringing together the creative voices of composer/performers James Moore (guitar & banjo)\, Caroline Shaw (violin)\, Nathan Koci (accordion)\, and Eleonore Oppenheim (bass). Drawing from an eclectic array of influences in classical\, jazz and folk traditions\, the group produces a unique and evocative blend of joyful melodies\, lush sonic textures and explosive improvisations. \nAbout Dance Heginbotham: Dance Heginbotham (DH) is a New York-based contemporary dance company committed to supporting\, producing\, and performing the work of choreographer John Heginbotham. With an emphasis on collaboration\, DH enriches national and international communities with its unique blend of inventive\, thoughtful\, and rigorous dance theater works. Founded in 2011\, DH had its world premiere in January 2012 at The Kennedy Center and has been presented by major venues throughout the US including Bard SummerScape\, Brooklyn Academy of Music\, Hopkins Center for the Arts\, Jacob’s Pillow Dance Festival\, The Joyce Theater\, Lincoln Center\, The Metropolitan Museum of Art\, and Works Process at The Guggenheim\, among many others. DH has shared the stage with luminaries of the music world including Alarm Will Sound\, Brooklyn Rider\, The Knights\, National Symphony Orchestra\, Joshua Bell\, André de Ridder\, and Eric Jacobsen\, and has commissioned new scores from composers Tyondai Braxton\, Ethan Iverson\, and Colin Jacobsen. DH has collaborated with designers and artists Maira Kalman\, Isaac Mizrahi\, Amy Trompetter\, Maile Okamura\, and Nicole Pearce in the creation of new works. \nwww.danceheginbotham.org
URL:https://www.peakperfs.org/event/the-party-scene/
CATEGORIES:2026 - 2027
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.peakperfs.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/party-scene.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Gcal Uumontclair Org 9Kptanknnvqcom49Ks44Nnaaak": "https://www.uumontclair.org/events"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_uumontclair_org_9kptanknnvqcom49ks44nnaaak
URL:https://www.uumontclair.org/events
SUMMARY:Poetry Covenant Group
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261122T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261122T210000
DTSTAMP:20260926T045408Z
UID:7v06gikiv7fa6bf85datbert29@google.com__20261122
SEQUENCE:7
CREATED:20200824T212257Z
DESCRIPTION:Led by UUCM member Patti Taylor\, this group is open to those 
 who enjoy reading poetry and sharing this love with others. After the read
 ing of each poem there is an opportunity for a discussion of the offering.
  These discussions may be short or long depending on how the group is move
 d. Bring your favorite poem to share with us and be prepared for a good ti
 me with this group. <br><br><a href="mailto:covenantgroups@uumontclair.or
 g" target="_blank">Contact for more information</a><p><br>─────
 ─────<br><br>UUCM A is inviting you to a scheduled Zoom meeting.
 <br><br>Join Zoom Meeting<br><a href="https://us06web.zoom.us/j/8585602169
